{"id": "EUVD-2026-59460", "enisaUuid": "4ff1a671-c4ca-3db7-9dce-053fd3f0d635", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvduse: hold vduse_lock across IDR lookup in open path\n\nvduse_dev_open() looks up struct vduse_dev through the IDR and then\nacquires dev->lock only after vduse_lock has been dropped.\n\nThis leaves a window where a concurrent VDUSE_DESTROY_DEV can remove the\nsame object from the IDR and free it before the open path locks the\ndevice, leading to a use-after-free.\n\nClose this race by keeping vduse_lock held until dev->lock has been\nacquired in the open path, matching the lock ordering already used by\nthe destroy path.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:32", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/35483c5306e09b3190ff937089d404a78012695c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c1560be8aa6849356455af67518d35c551cbd95", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/93ed4692f2299a40346025979f40e4a9b7b33af7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d94e2947203aead590fd63f667d316d4475d65af", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2d0a57538fd0b3b3ab75d64bb64f4cd2fab13a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/79e12c891940b0c4c75881b7fd82a8cbb8ac97be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e440e077748939839d9f76e24383b76b785f80ce"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74313", "GHSA-m274-mg38-f4wj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "27a1459b-2f59-3be5-ba0e-384d2edec155", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "2a2c988b-4593-3aab-8fa9-3265bf1b6bdc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8a6153b6c59d95c0e091f053f6f180952ade91e <e440e077748939839d9f76e24383b76b785f80ce"}, {"id": "360df003-b039-3821-b787-75df93577faf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8a6153b6c59d95c0e091f053f6f180952ade91e <d94e2947203aead590fd63f667d316d4475d65af"}, {"id": "50ba468a-c69d-3bff-88f5-564293a838f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "58a4f36e-7c8c-3b89-8dd5-9d7698e004db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5a573638-1bc3-39ee-9225-3d64164589e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8a6153b6c59d95c0e091f053f6f180952ade91e <93ed4692f2299a40346025979f40e4a9b7b33af7"}, {"id": "74011e58-ed69-3e5c-8f76-35fe3b5c42b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "7dc4a3ab-746f-3c2c-8627-f1ef4d38b62e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "820c5cba-4421-306b-aa52-fd0fda7efd7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "87feb6e7-9147-3caf-925d-e4487644f46d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8a6153b6c59d95c0e091f053f6f180952ade91e <79e12c891940b0c4c75881b7fd82a8cbb8ac97be"}, {"id": "8a6f8aa5-3ef8-340f-8894-5ff4cdd7fb9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "939701b8-7369-3fbd-b620-ff132037ce85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "a5f444fb-d199-37e4-a243-dd01e035497a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8a6153b6c59d95c0e091f053f6f180952ade91e <5c1560be8aa6849356455af67518d35c551cbd95"}, {"id": "c496d4ac-a70e-3e98-9e1c-adf556466215", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "e161579f-bafe-3b08-9160-a5c25ac14e6a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version